comments[4]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-29T00:20:04.660Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check: all-status PM search for Bun merge-driver drift found the closed package-runner dispatch issue pm-rnl3sa and other merge work, but no owner for this Bun-specific install/health mismatch."
  "2026-09-29T04:56:31.027Z","harness:codex","Test-audit contract: Bun-installed merge drivers must pass strict health, remain idempotent, and execute a real merge. Existing merge safety tests cover Node driver syntax and worktree identity, not Bun's executable name or bunx runtime path. Primary proof will use a disposable Git/Bun workspace."
  "2026-09-29T06:50:40.724Z","harness:codex","Acceptance evidence: actual Bun 1.4.2 in a disposable npm-packed consumer installed an absolute /usr/bin/bun merge driver; bunx --bun init and repeated merge install both passed strict health with zero findings. A real Git branch merge invoked item and history drivers, retained the left note and right description, and pm history --verify returned three valid entries. npx --no-install pm and bunx --no-install pm both returned the packed CLI version. Linked regression test passed; full suite 9414 passed; exact V8 coverage 100/100/100/100; pnpm quality:static passed. Repository source npm audit found zero advisories and GitHub open Dependabot, code, and secret scanning alerts were empty."
  "2026-09-29T06:58:37.384Z","harness:codex","Post-rebase packed acceptance on v2026.9.29: fresh tarball installed with Bun in a disposable Git project, bunx --bun pm init succeeded, bunx --bun pm health --strict-exit reported ok with zero findings, and both npx --no-install pm --version and bunx --no-install pm --version returned 2026.9.29. The earlier disposable project also completed a real semantic item/history Git merge with a verified chain."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-29T06:50:41.415Z","harness:codex",Bun can report a versioned executable path while Git later needs a durable absolute launcher; resolve and validate bun from absolute PATH entries at install time and audit both Node and Bun driver identities.
